s or evaluation. There are no significant errors.","questionText":"2. (a) Explain why a monopolistically competitive firm can make economic (abnormal) profit in the short run, but not in the long run.\b [10] (b) Discuss the consequences of a perfectly competitive market becoming a monopoly market.\b [15] Section B Answer one question from this section. Macroeconomics"},"secondarySubtopics":["Monopoly"],"secondaryTopicIds":[],"secondaryTopics":[],"session":"May","skills":["skill.analysis_chain_of_reasoning","skill.diagram_construct","skill.diagram_explain","skill.economic_terminology","skill.evaluation_tradeoffs","skill.explanation_causal_chain","skill.knowledge_definition","skill.stakeholder_analysis"],"solutionStatus":"Official IB markscheme image with extracted accessible transcript","sourceId":"ib-economics-hl:2021-may-tz1-hl-p1-q02","sourceLevels":["HL"],"sourceMarkSchemeUrl":"https://ibdocs.re/p/IB%20PAST%20PAPERS%20-%20YEAR/2021%20Examination%20Session/May%202021%20Examination%20Session/Individuals%20and%20societies/Economics_paper_1__TZ1_HL_markscheme.pdf","sourceQuestionUrl":"https://ibdocs.re/p/IB%20PAST%20PAPERS%20-%20YEAR/2021%20Examination%20Session/May%202021%20Examination%20Session/Individuals%20and%20societies/Economics_paper_1__TZ1_HL.pdf","sourceType":"actual_past_paper","sourceUrl":"https://ibdocs.re/p/IB%20PAST%20PAPERS%20-%20YEAR/2021%20Examination%20Session/May%202021%20Examination%20Session/Individuals%20and%20societies/Economics_paper_1__TZ1_HL.pdf","subject":"Economics","subpartEvidence":[{"detailed_subtopic_ids":["content.microeconomics.monopolistic-competition","content.microeconomics.monopoly"],"part_id":"(b)"},{"detailed_subtopic_ids":["content.microeconomics.monopolistic-competition"],"part_id":"(a)"}],"subtopics":["Monopolistic competition","Monopoly"],"summary":"2. (a) Explain why a monopolistically competitive firm can make economic (abnormal) profit in the short run, but not in the long run.\b [10] (b) Discuss the consequences of a p