 is limited understanding. 1 Any one from: • improves global monetary cooperation • promotes/oversee/monitor financial/monetary/macroeconomic stability • monitors/surveillance economic/financial policies/monetary systems • provides advice to countries in BOP/financial difficulties/on economic policies • provides funds/loans/debt relief to countries in BOP/ financial difficulties • provides economic forecasts/analyses • stabilize/monitor exchange rates • provide capacity building • technical assistance/financial services • promote international monetary cooperation • facilitate expansion/balanced growth of international trade • establish multilateral system of payments. 2 There is clear understanding. 2 Any two from: • improves global monetary cooperation • promotes/oversee/monitor financial/monetary/macroeconomic stability • monitors/surveillance economic/financial policies/monetary systems • provides advice to countries in BOP/financial difficulties/on economic policies • provides funds/loans/debt relief to countries in BOP/ financial difficulties • provides economic forecasts/analyses • stabilize/monitor exchange rates • provide capacity building • technical assistance/financial services • promote international monetary cooperation • facilitate expansion/balanced growth of international trade • establish multilateral system of payments. – 4 – M23/3/ECONO/HP2/ENG/TZ0/XX/M (ii) Define the term remittances indicated in bold in the text (Text A, paragraph 5). [2] Level Marks 0 The work does not meet a standard described by the descriptors below. 0 1 Vague definition. 1 The idea that it is money sent into or out of the country. 2 Accurate definition. 2 An understanding that it is the transfer of money/funds [1] from foreign/overseas workers to (individuals/households) their home country [1]. (b) (i) Using information from Table 1 and Table 2, calculate the value of Mexico’s gross domestic product (GDP) (in US$) in 2019. [2] 10267 x 128 Any valid working should be rewar