ry. Available at: https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/jan/12/ australia-needs-to-rethink-papua-new-guinea-aid-people-need-power-and-water-not-governance-workshops [Accessed 1 August 2024]. Source adapted. Text E Dickenson-Jones, G., and Wijeweera, A., 2010. An empirical analysis of price and income elasticities of Papua New Guinea’s exports. In: Pacific Economic Bulletin, Volume 25 Number 2. [online] Available at: https://openresearch-repository.anu.edu.au/items/c6d3323f-b3d2-43a2-b795-a4e285bdf314 [Accessed 1 August 2024]. Pp. 140–151. Source adapted. Laveil, M., 2023. PNG’s trade ties with China are set to strengthen. The Interpreter, The Lowy Institute, [online] 8 June. Available at: https://www.lowyinstitute.org/the-interpreter/png-s-trade-ties-china-are-set-strengthen [Accessed 1 August 2024]. Source adapted. Text F International Trade Administration, n.d. Papua New Guinea – Country Commercial Guide – Market Overview. [online] Available at: https://www.trade.gov/country-commercial-guides/papua-new-guinea-market- overview?section-nav=11960 [Accessed 1 August 2024]. Source adapted. Table 4 The World Bank Group, n.d. Papua New Guinea – Overview. [online] Available at: https://data.worldbank.org/ country/papua-new-guinea [Accessed 1 August 2024]. Source adapted. International Monetary Fund, 2023. IMF Country Report No. 23/385 – Papua New Guinea. [online] Available at: https://www.elibrary.imf.org/view/journals/002/2023/385/article-A000-en.xml [Accessed 1 August 2024]. Source adapted. United Nations Development Programme, 2024. Human Development Reports – Papua New Guinea. [online] Available at: https://hdr.undp.org/data-center/specific-country-data#/countries/PNG [Accessed 1 August 2024]. Source adapted. Table 5 International Monetary Fund, 2023. IMF Country Report No. 23/385 – Papua New Guinea. [online] Available at: https://www.elibrary.imf.org/view/journals/002/2023/385/article-A000-en.xml [Accessed 1 August 2024]. Source adapted. Figure 1 The World B